WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:16.434
Hi! A caterpillar turns into a butterfly, and a tadpole turns into a frog. Living things pass through different stages in their lives. This is a life cycle. Let's review life cycles from Primary 3.

2
00:00:16.584 --> 00:00:21.138
A butterfly starts life as an egg, usually laid on a leaf.

3
00:00:21.288 --> 00:00:27.762
The egg hatches into a larva, the caterpillar. It eats leaves all the time and grows quickly.

4
00:00:27.912 --> 00:00:34.458
Then it becomes a pupa. The pupa does not eat or move, while its body changes inside.

5
00:00:34.608 --> 00:00:46.242
Finally, the adult butterfly comes out. It lays eggs, and the cycle starts again. Mosquitoes, beetles and houseflies also have these four stages.

6
00:00:46.392 --> 00:00:52.362
Cockroaches and grasshoppers have only three stages: egg, nymph and adult.

7
00:00:52.512 --> 00:01:01.554
A nymph looks like a small adult, but it has no wings. It moults, or sheds its skin, several times as it grows.

8
00:01:01.704 --> 00:01:11.610
A frog's eggs hatch in water into tadpoles, which breathe with gills. A tadpole slowly grows legs, becomes a froglet, and then an adult frog.

9
00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.882
A chicken has three stages: egg, chick and adult.

10
00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:25.098
A flowering plant grows from a seed into a seedling, then into an adult plant that has flowers and fruits. The fruits hold new seeds.

11
00:01:25.248 --> 00:01:34.842
When the seedling is young, its seed leaves give it food. So the seed leaves get smaller and smaller, and finally drop off.

12
00:01:34.992 --> 00:01:39.378
Watch out! Not every insect has a pupa stage!

13
00:01:39.528 --> 00:01:45.282
Butterflies and mosquitoes have four: egg, larva, pupa and adult.

14
00:01:45.432 --> 00:01:53.154
Cockroaches and grasshoppers have three: egg, nymph and adult, with no pupa.

15
00:01:53.304 --> 00:02:02.010
Your turn! Which stage of the butterfly does not eat? Pause and think.

16
00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:10.242
The pupa. It does not eat or move while its body changes inside. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:10.392 --> 00:02:19.578
Another one! Where do the larvae and pupae of mosquitoes live? Pause and think.

18
00:02:19.728 --> 00:02:29.898
In water. That's why we empty stagnant water from flower pots and containers, so mosquitoes can't breed. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:30.048 --> 00:02:39.642
Last one! Why do a seedling's seed leaves get smaller and smaller? Pause and think.

20
00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:49.866
Because the seedling uses up the food stored in them. Once its own leaves can make food, the seed leaves fall off. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:50.016 --> 00:03:01.818
Remember: butterflies and mosquitoes have four stages: egg, larva, pupa and adult. Cockroaches and grasshoppers have three: egg, nymph and adult.

22
00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:09.930
A frog passes through tadpole and froglet stages, and a plant grows from a seed into a seedling and then an adult plant.

23
00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:16.386
Next time you see a caterpillar in the park, think about which stage it's in!

